* verifier si wsl tourne:

  wsl --list --verbose

* networking

# Windows Defender Firewall
New-NetFirewallRule -DisplayName "WSL SSH" -Direction Inbound -Protocol TCP -LocalPort 12666 -Action Allow

# Hyper-V firewall (applies to WSL in mirrored mode)
New-NetFirewallHyperVRule -Name "WSL-SSH" -DisplayName "WSL SSH" -Direction Inbound `
  -VMCreatorId '{40E0AC32-46A5-438A-A0B2-2B479E8F2E90}' -Protocol TCP -LocalPorts 12666


WSL shuts down a little while after your last terminal closes, and then SSH stops working. A simple fix is a Task Scheduler task that runs at logon with:

wsl.exe -d Ubuntu -- sleep infinity


  wsl --shutdown


